From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 May 2026 00:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] PlatformObjectRegistry: tolerate duplicate registrations

In conda-forge's systemlib build of TensorFlow the same process loads
multiple shared objects that each statically embed the same
stream_executor registrar translation units, e.g.

  third_party/xla/xla/stream_executor/cuda/repeat_buffer_kernel_cuda.cc
    GPU_KERNEL_REGISTRY_REGISTER_KERNEL_STATICALLY(RepeatBufferKernelCuda, ...)

compiled into both libtensorflow_framework.so.2 and
libtensorflow_cc.so.2.21.0 (the latter loaded via the pywrap chain at
`import tensorflow`). PlatformObjectRegistry::GetGlobalRegistry() is a
single process-wide singleton, but every .so that contains the registrar
runs that registrar's module initializer once when it is loaded, so the
second and later identical registrations reach RegisterObject() and the
flat_hash_map insert returns inserted == false.

The registrar macros (STREAM_EXECUTOR_REGISTER_OBJECT_STATICALLY and
GPU_KERNEL_REGISTRY_REGISTER_KERNEL_STATICALLY) treat any non-OK status
from RegisterObject() as fatal:

  F0000 repeat_buffer_kernel_cuda.cc:32] Failed to register kernel:
    ALREADY_EXISTS: Object for trait
    ...GpuKernelRegistry...RepeatBufferKernel... and platform CUDA is
    already registered.
  *** Check failure stack trace: ***  -> Aborted (core dumped)

so `import tensorflow` aborts before it finishes initializing.

The registry's contract is that registered objects are immutable and
cannot be overwritten, and these duplicates originate from the same
statically-compiled registrar, so they are identical. Keep the first
registration and report success for an identical-key duplicate instead
of returning AlreadyExistsError. Fixing it here, at the single insert
chokepoint, covers GPU kernels and every other
STREAM_EXECUTOR_REGISTER_OBJECT_STATICALLY user without having to patch
each registrar macro. This mirrors the OpRegistry duplicate-tolerance
patch used elsewhere in this feedstock.
---
--- a/third_party/xla/xla/stream_executor/platform/platform_object_registry.cc
+++ b/third_party/xla/xla/stream_executor/platform/platform_object_registry.cc
@@ -70,9 +70,18 @@
   const auto [it, inserted] = objects_.insert(std::make_pair(
       std::make_tuple(std::type_index(type), platform_id), std::move(object)));
   if (!inserted) {
-    return absl::AlreadyExistsError(absl::StrFormat(
-        "Object for trait %s and platform %s is already registered.",
-        type.name(), GetPlatformName(platform_id)));
+    // conda-forge: TensorFlow is split across several shared objects
+    // (libtensorflow_framework.so, libtensorflow_cc.so,
+    // _pywrap_tensorflow_internal.so). Each .so that contains a
+    // STREAM_EXECUTOR_REGISTER_OBJECT_STATICALLY / GPU_KERNEL_REGISTRY_
+    // REGISTER_KERNEL_STATICALLY registrar runs that registrar's module
+    // initializer once when it is loaded into the process, so the second
+    // and later registrations of the same (trait, platform) reach this
+    // singleton registry. Registered objects are immutable and these
+    // duplicates come from the same statically-compiled registrar, so they
+    // are identical; keep the first and treat the duplicate as success
+    // rather than aborting via the registrar macro's LOG(FATAL).
+    return absl::OkStatus();
   }
   return absl::OkStatus();
 }
